{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659756",
      "title": "Setting Component Types Dynamically",
      "sourceHash": "3c733cbe6440e6d0475fe4ed0ebcca35f0e7dd0305281f48639d33eea00559e2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "Now with that Tabs component added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 6.39,
          "en": "there's one other thing I wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.39,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "with that component and one other concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "and pattern I wanna explore together with you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 17.27,
          "en": "And this extra concept is related to this menu element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 18.303,
          "en": "in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 20.34,
          "en": "In this Tabs component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.34,
          "end": 23.07,
          "en": "we might wanna wrap our buttons with a menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.07,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "but maybe we wanna make this Tabs component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "a bit more flexible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 29.76,
          "en": "And if it is being used in different parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.76,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "of the application, which is not the case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "but which could be the case in bigger applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 39.93,
          "en": "we might want to be able to use different wrapper elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.93,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "around our buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 44.013,
          "en": "in those different places in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "Now, one way, of course, would be to simply get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 49.18,
          "en": "of the menu here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "and to then use the elements that we wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "as a wrapper here in the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 57.963,
          "en": "where we're setting the buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.92,
          "end": 61.66,
          "en": "Now, this would be one way of solving this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.76,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "but a different way, which is maybe more elegant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "is to keep using this wrapper element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "because this also ensures that this separation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "between our buttons and the content is always enforced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "But we might want to allow the developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.99,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "to choose which wrapper element should be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "if the Tabs component is used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 89.43,
          "en": "in different places of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.43,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "And for that, we could accept an additional prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 94.803,
          "en": "that could be named buttonsContainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.75999999999999,
          "end": 97.92,
          "en": "Though the name, of course, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.92,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "But the idea here behind this prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "is to get the element that should be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 109.25,
          "en": "as a wrapper so that in Examples.jsx, I can go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.32,
          "end": 113.52000000000001,
          "en": "to the Tabs component and set this buttonsContainer prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.52000000000001,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "which I just added in my destructuring code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 118.62,
          "en": "in the Tabs.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.62,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "And then maybe here, set this to menu",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "if I wanna use the menu element or ul",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 127.74,
          "en": "if I wanna use the unordered list element instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 129.64,
          "en": "or div if I wanna use a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "or maybe even a custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 136.56,
          "en": "like the Section component if I would want to use this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.56,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "So I basically want to be able to use the identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "of a component as a value for this prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "not the component itself with those angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 152.78,
          "en": "but just the identifier, like for example, menu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 156.87,
          "en": "And there is an important difference between built-in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.87,
          "end": 160.07999999999998,
          "en": "and custom components, which you could already see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 164.34,
          "en": "Custom components must be passed as a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "so to say like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 170.583,
          "en": "So with curly braces, and then your function name like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.51,
          "end": 174.6,
          "en": "But for built-in elements like menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.6,
          "end": 176.34,
          "en": "you're not doing it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.34,
          "end": 179.91,
          "en": "because that would look for a variable named menu",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.91,
          "end": 180.93,
          "en": "in your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.93,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "and try to pass the value stored in such a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 187.89,
          "en": "as a value for this buttonsContainer prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.89,
          "end": 192.1,
          "en": "And I don't have a variable named menu in my code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.26,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "but instead for built-in elements like menu or div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 200.523,
          "en": "you simply pass the identifier as a string like this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 204.69,
          "en": "So that's an important difference here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.69,
          "end": 207.45,
          "en": "But how can we now use this buttonsContainer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.45,
          "end": 210.21,
          "en": "that contains this component identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 212.073,
          "en": "inside of the Tabs component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 214.62,
          "en": "Well, we could try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "to simply replace the hard-coded menu element identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 224.22,
          "en": "between those angle brackets here with buttonsContainer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 228.9,
          "en": "so with that prop name here, but this wouldn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 230.49,
          "en": "Instead, this would be looking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 235.41,
          "en": "for a built-in element called buttonsContainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.41,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "And I'm talking about a built-in component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 239.22,
          "en": "because it's starting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.22,
          "end": 241.59,
          "en": "with a lowercase character, but of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.59,
          "end": 244.92,
          "en": "there is no built-in component called buttonsContainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.92,
          "end": 247.5,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna use the value that's received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.5,
          "end": 252.18,
          "en": "on this buttonsContainer prop here as an identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.18,
          "end": 256.17,
          "en": "So what we have to do here to make sure that instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.17,
          "end": 259.83,
          "en": "of looking for a built-in component named buttonsContainer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.83,
          "end": 263.61,
          "en": "it takes a look at the value inside of this prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.61,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "and treats that as a custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.14,
          "en": "which should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.14,
          "end": 271.74,
          "en": "We have to add a special const or a variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.74,
          "end": 273.81,
          "en": "which could be named Buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.81,
          "end": 277.35,
          "en": "or ButtonContainer like this, but which starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.35,
          "end": 280.14300000000003,
          "en": "with a capital case character, that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.1,
          "end": 283.53,
          "en": "And then here in this ButtonsContainer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.53,
          "end": 285.933,
          "en": "we could store this buttonsContainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.58,
          "end": 290.22,
          "en": "So with that, we're basically creating a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.22,
          "end": 291.96,
          "en": "or constant in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.96,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "which can be used as a custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 297.93,
          "en": "because it starts with an uppercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.93,
          "end": 300.483,
          "en": "and which can therefore be used here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.47,
          "end": 305.28,
          "en": "And now what React will do here is it will take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.28,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "at the value stored in buttonsContainer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 310.08,
          "en": "and that will, of course, be the value received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.08,
          "end": 311.853,
          "en": "on this buttonsContainer prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.02,
          "end": 316.38,
          "en": "And it will then either see that it's a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.38,
          "end": 319.11,
          "en": "and in that case, it will try to look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.11,
          "end": 322.17,
          "en": "for a built-in component that can be identified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.17,
          "end": 324.54,
          "en": "by that string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.54,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "Or if we would pass in a custom component like section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 330.84,
          "en": "React would also recognize that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.84,
          "end": 332.34000000000003,
          "en": "and see that we're not trying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.34000000000003,
          "end": 334.77,
          "en": "to output some built-in component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.77,
          "end": 336.45,
          "en": "but that we're instead trying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 336.45,
          "end": 339.42,
          "en": "to display some custom component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.42,
          "end": 341.55,
          "en": "and it would then render that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.55,
          "end": 344.553,
          "en": "It would call that component function, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.2,
          "end": 350.073,
          "en": "But in this case, I wanna stick to this string identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.42,
          "end": 355.5,
          "en": "And with that, if we save that, if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 355.5,
          "end": 360.5,
          "en": "this all works snd if we inspect our tabs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.08,
          "end": 362.64,
          "en": "we can also still see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 362.64,
          "end": 365.283,
          "en": "that there is this menu element being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 366.3,
          "end": 367.89,
          "en": "And we could now, on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 367.89,
          "end": 370.95,
          "en": "also replace menu here with div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 370.95,
          "end": 373.41,
          "en": "And if I save that, we don't just see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 374.85,
          "en": "that the styling is broken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 374.85,
          "end": 377.76,
          "en": "because the menu element was actually used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 377.76,
          "end": 379.59,
          "en": "in some CSS rules here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 379.59,
          "end": 383.31,
          "en": "but we also see that indeed, here we have a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.31,
          "end": 385.89300000000003,
          "en": "as a wrapper around these buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 386.97,
          "end": 388.41,
          "en": "And with that, we're now able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.41,
          "end": 391.8,
          "en": "to dynamically set the wrapper that should be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 391.8,
          "end": 393.3,
          "en": "around these buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 393.3,
          "end": 395.7,
          "en": "when we're using this Tabs component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 395.7,
          "end": 398.37,
          "en": "Here I'll go back to using a menu",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 398.37,
          "end": 400.56,
          "en": "but knowing about this pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 400.56,
          "end": 405,
          "en": "where you essentially pass a component identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 405,
          "end": 407.07,
          "en": "as a value for a prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.07,
          "end": 409.53,
          "en": "and you're then using this identifier inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 409.53,
          "end": 414.09000000000003,
          "en": "of a component to dynamically render different HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 414.09000000000003,
          "end": 417.183,
          "en": "is another crucial concept you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 418.32,
          "end": 421.23,
          "en": "And of course, here we could have also taken some shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 421.23,
          "end": 425.64,
          "en": "and instead of remapping this prop to some constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 425.64,
          "end": 428.13,
          "en": "we could have simply accepted a prop that starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 428.13,
          "end": 429.573,
          "en": "with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 431.37,
          "end": 432.54,
          "en": "We then just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 432.54,
          "end": 436.56,
          "en": "that we also set this prop with an uppercase character here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 436.56,
          "end": 439.5,
          "en": "in the place where we're using this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 439.5,
          "end": 442.89,
          "en": "And with that, we would achieve the same result as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 442.89,
          "end": 446.64,
          "en": "So now here I got the menu back, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 446.64,
          "end": 448.68,
          "en": "But this is a crucial pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 448.68,
          "end": 451.92,
          "en": "And whilst it might be confusing at first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 451.92,
          "end": 452.753,
          "en": "it's, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 452.753,
          "end": 455.67,
          "en": "simply about receiving a component identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 455.67,
          "end": 457.47,
          "en": "as a value for a prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 457.47,
          "end": 460.89,
          "en": "And the only two important things to remember here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 460.89,
          "end": 464.04,
          "en": "is that that prop then must be usable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 464.04,
          "end": 467.43,
          "en": "as a custom component in the receiving component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 467.43,
          "end": 470.13,
          "en": "So the tabs component in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 470.13,
          "end": 472.77,
          "en": "So it must start with an uppercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 472.77,
          "end": 476.28,
          "en": "or it must be remapped to a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 476.28,
          "end": 480.15,
          "en": "or a variable that starts with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 480.15,
          "end": 483.33,
          "en": "And the other important thing is that when it comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 483.33,
          "end": 487.68,
          "en": "to these identifiers, you use string names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 487.68,
          "end": 492.31,
          "en": "for the built-in elements like menu, ul or div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 493.68,
          "end": 498.68,
          "en": "and you use your component functions like this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 498.75,
          "end": 501.51,
          "en": "if you wanna use a custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 501.51,
          "end": 503.82,
          "en": "You're not calling the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 503.82,
          "end": 508.82,
          "en": "and you're not using it with angle brackets like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 508.86,
          "end": 511.74,
          "en": "Instead, you're just using the function name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 511.74,
          "end": 513.81,
          "en": "if you wanna pass the identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 513.81,
          "end": 517.74,
          "en": "for a custom component as a prop value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 517.74,
          "end": 520.11,
          "en": "But here it's this string identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 520.11,
          "end": 522.993,
          "en": "because I wanna use the built-in menu component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
